    <div>
      <div class="sec-head" style="margin-bottom:0"><p class="q">Why would I need it?</p><h2 class="h2">Whoever keeps the book keeps the history.</h2></div>
      <div class="story">
        <div class="beat"><span class="dot">Oct</span><p>You pay your landlord <span class="num">UGX 450,000</span> for October, in cash.</p></div>
        <div class="beat"><span class="dot">Dec</span><p>In December he says October never came.</p></div>
        <div class="beat last"><span class="dot">Now</span><p>Your word against his, and his receipt book, in his handwriting.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="lbl" style="margin-top:clamp(56px,7vw,88px)">What people use today</p>
  <div class="today2">
    <div class="obj2"><div class="art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="unsigned">Unsigned</span><div class="nb"><p>David 450k</p><p>Oct, cash</p><p>Nov, cash</p></div></div><p class="nm">A notebook</p></div>
    <div class="obj2"><div class="art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="unsigned">Unsigned</span><div class="mini-wa">Sent the October rent to you<small>10:21 ✓✓</small></div></div><p class="nm">A WhatsApp message</p></div>
    <div class="obj2"><div class="art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="unsigned">Unsigned</span><div class="cloud">I think I paid him&hellip;</div></div><p class="nm">Memory</p></div>
    <div class="obj2"><div class="art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="unsigned">Unsigned</span><div class="sms"><b>MOBILE MONEY</b>You have sent UGX 450,000 to DAVID J. on 01/10/2026.</div></div><p class="nm">A Mobile Money SMS</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="today-cap" data-new="1">A notebook, a message and memory are written by one side. A Mobile Money SMS comes from the network. Neither of you signed any of them.</p>

  <p class="closer-line">Only one side ever gets to write it down. <span data-new="1">With Sawaza, both sides hold it, signed.</span></p>
